            Hey, page creator! I hope you don't mind, but I made some changes, like using the with-induction version that was in the paper, moving some stuff around a bit, and removing a couple of non-models. I did my best to not delete what you wrote unless it contained an error I couldn't fix. (The model on `2 x N + 1` didn't satisfy axiom 3, for example.)
            The source for the previous version is still available if you want to use it for future edits:
            https://ncatlab.org/nlab/source/Nelson+arithmetic/9
            
            If someone else sees this after like June 2022, feel free to delete it. I just don't want the possibly-a-new-contributor to think their work wasn't cared about and permanently deleted.
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An extension of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peano+arithmetic"} Peano arithmetic
            as described in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Nelson"} Edward Nelson’s paper
          %h2#definition  Definition
          %p
            Nelson arithmetic (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi NA
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NA
            ) is expressed in the language with a constant
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            and binary functions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdot
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peano+arithmetic"} Peano arithmetic
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi x
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_x \neg s(x) = 0
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{x, y} (s(x) = s(y)) \Rightarrow (x = y)
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_x x + 0 = x
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{x, y} x + s(y) = s(x+y)
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_x x \cdot 0 = 0
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi y
                      %mo +
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{x, y} x \cdot s(y) = x \cdot y + x
                ;
            %li
              %p
                For any predicate
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
                in first-order logic in the language
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⋅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdot
                (but
                %i not
                containing
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mo ∀
                          %mi x
                        %mi φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Sx
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇒
                        %msub
                          %mo ∀
                          %mi x
                        %mi φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi(0) \wedge (\forall_x  \varphi(x) \Rightarrow \varphi(Sx)) \Rightarrow \forall_x \varphi(x)
          %p
            with the two additional axioms regarding
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(0)
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi x
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{x} \mathcal{C}(x) \Rightarrow \mathcal{C}(s(x))
                ;
          %p
            We may choose to omit the axiom schema (7), in which case we refer to
            %i Nelson arithmetic without induction
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi NA
                  %mo −
                  %mi Ind
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NA-Ind
            ). Without induction, it is not possible to prove that addition or multiplication are commutative or associative. Optionally, we could add the axiom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi x
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ∨
                  %msub
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi y
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_x x = 0 \vee \exists_y x = s(y)
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robinson+arithmetic"} Robinson arithmetic
            so that the resulting theory extends Robinson arithmetic, however we don’t in this page.
          %h3#counting_numbers Counting numbers
          %p
            The predicate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is supposed to refer to “counting numbers”, in the familiar intuitive sense that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            are supposed to be for counting. Nelson states in his paper that
          %blockquote
            %p
              It follows (…) that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SS
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SS0
          %p
            And indeed, there are many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+model+of+arithmetic"} non-standard models of Nelson arithmetic
            where not every number in the model is a “counting number”/“natural number”. Unfortunately, nonstandard models of Peano arithmetic, which Nelson arithmetic extends, are hard to describe, and cannot have computable arithmetic operations.
          %p
            Nonstandard models of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi NA
                  %mo −
                  %mi Ind
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NA-Ind
            are more common though. If one has any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+ring"} ordered ring
            R (meaning
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is partially ordered with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +
            monotone,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq 0
            are closed under multiplication), then the subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mi r
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{\geq 0} = \{r \in R \mid r \geq 0\}
            is a model of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi NA
                    %mo −
                    %mi Ind
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NA-Ind
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(a)
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \{0, 1, 1+1, 1+1+1, \cdots\}
            (the image of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            under the unique ring homomorphism
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \to R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}_{\geq 0}
            and nonnegative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
            both produce models in this way.
          %p
            On the other extreme, one could define a model where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(a)
            is true for all numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            in the model, and thus all number trivially are “counting numbers”, though in that case the “counting numbers” interpretation of the predicate doesn’t make much intuitive sense anymore.
          %h3#additionable_multiplicable_and_exponentiable_numbers Additionable, multiplicable, and exponentiable numbers
          %p
            We define the unary predicate
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}(x)
            if for all counting numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo +
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y + x
            is also a counting number. Similarly, we define the unary predicate
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}(x)
            if for all additionable numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \cdot x
            is also an additionable number. Without induction, we don’t know that addition of “additionable numbers” or multiplication of “multiplicable numbers” is associative.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\uparrow(-)
            denote the exponentiation function; if we aren’t using induction, instead suppose that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+function"} binary function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi N
                  %mo ×
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\uparrow(-):N \times N \to N
            called “exponentiation” such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \uparrow 0 = s(0)
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \uparrow s(y) = x \cdot x \uparrow y
          %p Nelson states that
          %blockquote
            %p
              If we attempt to define “exponentiable number” in the same spirit, we are unable to prove that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_2
              are exponentiable numbers then so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1 \uparrow x_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                    %mn 3
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                    %mn 3
                    %mo =
                    %mn 64
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2 \uparrow 2) \uparrow 3 = 4 \uparrow 3 = 64
              whereas
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mn 8
                      %mo =
                      %mn 256
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \uparrow (2 \uparrow 3) = 2 \uparrow 8 = 256
          %h4#categorification Categorification
          %p
            The categorification of Nelson’s argument would proceed as follows: Suppose we have the subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CountSet
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi FinSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CountSet \hookrightarrow FinSet
            of the category of finite sets whose cardinality is a counting number. (Here “finite” refers to the internal notion, not the external notion. Although our language only contains numbers, not sets, we can encode this category in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PA
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PA
            using a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FinSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet
            where objects are (internal) natural numbers and a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo →
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \to n
            is encoded as a natural number less than
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi n
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^m
          %p
            Then we can form a further subcategory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi AddSet
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi CountSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AddSet \hookrightarrow CountSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that the coproduct
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A + C
            exists in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ContSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ContSet
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ContSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ContSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CountSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CountSet
            may not have had binary coproducts,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AddSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AddSet
            has binary coproducts.
          %p
            Next, we can form a further subcategory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MultSet
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi CountSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MultSet \hookrightarrow CountSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            such that the product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \times A
            exists in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AddSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AddSet
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi AddSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AddSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AddSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AddSet
            may not have had binary products,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MultSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MultSet
            has binary products.
          %p
            Now, we can form a further subcategory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ExpSet
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi MultSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ExpSet \hookrightarrow MultSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            such that the exponent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^E
            exists in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MultSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MultSet
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MultSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MultSet
            i.e. the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentiable+object"} exponentiable object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MultSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MultSet
            %i cannot
            prove that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ExpSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ExpSet
            has exponents (hence can’t prove that it’s
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed"} cartesian closed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CE%A0-pretopos"} Π-pretopos
          %h3#ultrafinitism Ultrafinitism
          %p
            The theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi NA
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NA
          %p
            Categorifying the current axioms to the category of sets, the counting sets (represented by the sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            in which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(S)
            is
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited"} inhabited
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal"} symmetric monoidal
            with respect to either the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            or the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            %span.newWikiWord
              CountSet
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/CountSet"} ?
            forms a framework of mathematics, which is sometimes called “ultrafinite mathematics”, that is significantly weaker than
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} strongly predicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+mathematics"} finite mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategories"} subcategories
            of additionable finite sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AddSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AddSet
            and multiplicable finite sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MultSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MultSet
            can be proven to be symmetric monoidal.
          %h2#models_of_nelson_arithmetic Models of Nelson arithmetic
          %p
            A model of Nelson arithmetic is a model of Peano arithmetic
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (N,0,S,+,\cdot)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset N
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in C
            implies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(a) \in C
          %p
            A model of Nelson arithmetic without induction is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            with an element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in N
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:N \to N
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi N
                  %mo ×
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)+(-):N \times N \to N
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi N
                    %mo ×
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\cdot(-):N \times N \to N
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo :
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}:N \to \mathrm{Prop}
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg s(x) = 0
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(x) = s(y)
                implies
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + 0 = x
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + s(y) = s(x+y)
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \cdot 0 = 0
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi y
                      %mo +
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \cdot s(y) = x \cdot y + x
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(0)
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(x)
                implies
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(s(x))
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of models of Nelson arithmetic without induction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N^{'}
            is a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi N
                    %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:N \to N^{'}
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mn 0
                        %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 0
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi N
                            %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(0_N) = 0_{N^{'}}
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_N(x)
                implies
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi N
                            %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{N^{'}}(f(x))
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi N
                            %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(s_N(x)) = s_{N^{'}}(f(x))
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo +
                        %mi N
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo +
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi N
                            %mo ′
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x +_N y) = f(x) +_{N^{'}} f(y)
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in N
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi N
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi N
                            %mo ′
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x \cdot_N y) = f(x) \cdot_{N^{'}} f(y)
          %p
            Homomorphisms of models of Nelson arithmetic with induction are defined in the same way, but as with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PA
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PA
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+embedding"} elementary embedding
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of models of Nelson arithmetic without induction in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            is the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} NelsonArithmetics
                    %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{NelsonArithmetics}_\mathcal{U}
            whose objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} NelsonArithmetics
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob(\mathrm{NelsonArithmetics}_\mathcal{U})
            are the
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} NelsonArithmetics
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Ob(\mathrm{NelsonArithmetics}_\mathcal{U})
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} NelsonArithmetics
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in Ob(\mathrm{NelsonArithmetics}_\mathcal{U})
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Mor
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} NelsonArithmetics
                        %mi 𝒰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor_{\mathrm{NelsonArithmetics}_\mathcal{U}}(A, B)
            are the homomorphisms of models of Nelson arithmetic as defined above.
          %p
            This category is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+finiteness"} axiom of finiteness
            (meaning it thinks every set is finite), then (because there are no finite models of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi NA
                    %mo −
                    %mi Ind
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NA-Ind
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} NelsonArithmetics
                    %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{NelsonArithmetics}_\mathcal{U}
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+category"} empty
          %h3#example_models Example models
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                is the standard model of Nelson arithmetic, and is the initial model of Nelson arithmetic in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of models of Nelson arithmetic.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +1 : R \to R\setminus\{0\}
                is (total and) injective, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a model of Nelson arithmetic without induction, where we may take
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi r
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(r) = r + 1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                to be any of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : \mathbb{N} \to R
                defined by
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(0) = 0
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(n+1) = i(n)+1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in C
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi a
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in C \Rightarrow a + 1 \in C
            %li
              %p
                The set of non-negative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}_{\geq 0}
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi q
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(q) \coloneqq q + 1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(q)
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \in \mathbb{Q}_{\geq 0}
                is a model of Nelson arithmetic without induction.
            %li
              %p
                The set of non-negative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi r
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(r) \coloneqq r + 1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(r)
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
                is a model of Nelson arithmetic without induction.
            %li
              %p
                The subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \subset \mathbb{Z}[x]
                of polynomials with leading coefficient nonnegative
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"}
                  commutative
                  = succeed "-algebra" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                on a generating set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi r
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(r) \coloneqq r + 1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(r)
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{N}[S]
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                set
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo +
                        %mi 𝟙
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N} + \mathbb{1}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝟙
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *:\mathbb{1}
                is the unique element of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                with:
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(*) = *
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∀
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo .
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mi a
                          %mo =
                          %mo *
                          %mo =
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                          %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall a \in \mathbb{N}. * + a = * = a + *
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mo *
                          %mo =
                          %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * + * = *
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∀
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo .
                          %mo *
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi a
                          %mo =
                          %mi a
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall a \in \mathbb{N}. * \cdot a = a
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∀
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo +
                          %mi 𝟙
                          %mo .
                          %mi a
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo *
                          %mo =
                          %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall a \in \mathbb{N} + \mathbb{1}. a \cdot * = *
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(*)
              %p
                This defines a model of Nelson arithmetic without induction. Note that multiplication is not commutative and that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo *
                        %mo =
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \cdot * = *
            %li
              %p
                Given any nonstandard model
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                of Peano arithmetic, and any subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset N
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in C
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi a
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in C \Rightarrow a+1 \in C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                together give a model of Nelson arithmetic.
          %h2#groupoidal_categorification Groupoidal categorification
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoidal+categorification"} groupoidal categorification
            of Nelson arithmetic without induction is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            with
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in \mathcal{G}
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S:\mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{G}
            %li
              %p
                a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒢
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)+(-):\mathcal{G} \times \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{G}
            %li
              %p
                a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒢
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\cdot(-):\mathcal{G} \times \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{G}
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{G}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S(A) \cong 0) \to \emptyset
                from the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(A) \cong 0
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B \in \mathcal{G}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S(A) \cong S(B)) \to (A \cong B)
                from the set of isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(A) \cong S(B)
                to the set of isomorphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cong B
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{G}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A + 0 \cong A
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B \in \mathcal{G}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A + S(B) \cong S(A+B)
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{G}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cdot 0 \cong A
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B \in \mathcal{G}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi B
                      %mo +
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cdot S(B) \cong A \cdot B + A
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "-valued" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}:\mathcal{G} \to \mathrm{Set}
            %li
              %p
                an element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in \mathcal{C}(0)
            %li
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{G}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_A:\mathcal{C}(A) \to \mathcal{C}(S(A))
